    {
      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "contentPreview": "THE FIX SHAPE, and why it beat the obvious one. The deep dive that reproduced C1 proposed widening the lock around SaveIndexUnsafe\u0027s orphan sweep. That was rejected: import ADDS and OVERWRITES and never removes, so the sweep is not a capability it needs -- it is the mechanism that destroyed the data. \u0060SaveIndexUnsafe\u0060 was split into \u0060DeleteOrphanedSidecars \u002B PublishIndexUnsafe\u0060, and import now calls only the latter. Containment argument that made this safe: SaveIndexUnsafe has exactly ONE entry",
